import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations
import QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge

/-!
# The word filtration is not the ideal-power filtration

`prop:curvature-rank-gb-stratification` supplies the *word* side of the
word-depth ↔ partition-depth bridge (bean `wpdb`):

    J^r(q) / J^{r+1}(q) = { T_w : r(T_w) = r }

and four content blocks plus one compute script read the *partition* side —
`Z^{(k)}(A) = span{ e_λ : gbDepth λ = k }` — off it. The audit
[`2026-08-16-word-depth-vs-partition-depth-bridge-is-unstated`](../../../../../docs/audits/2026-08-16-word-depth-vs-partition-depth-bridge-is-unstated.md)
established that nothing in the corpus relates the two indexings.

This file rules out one of the three inequivalent things the corpus calls
`J^•` — and it is one the corpus **asserts**, not one nobody wrote down.

## Corrected framing (2026-08-16, same day as first landing)

This docstring originally called the ideal-power reading *"the tempting
reading"* and *"the one reading that would make them relate for free"*, as
though it were a hypothetical the corpus had never committed to. **That was an
under-claim, and correcting it upward matters more than the retractions
elsewhere in this PR.** Step 2 of
[`prf:curvature-rank-gb-stratification`](../../../mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification-proof.md)
asserts it outright:

> *"The filtration `J^ℓ(q)` collects elements requiring at least `ℓ`
> applications of these relations to reach normal form. **Equivalently, `J^ℓ` is
> the image of `I^ℓ` (the `ℓ`-th power of the rewrite ideal) under the quotient
> map.**"*

The two halves of that sentence are not equivalent, and the second is what the
theorems below kill. I had read the statement block and not the proof block.

## The reading, and why it is the tempting one

`H_n(R, q)` is presented as `R⟨σ_1, …, σ_{n-1}⟩ / I` with `I` generated by the
braid and Hecke relations. Given that presentation the ideal-power candidate is
canonical, is a genuine filtration by two-sided ideals, and needs no extra data.
If it worked, the bridge would be a computation rather than a conjecture — which
is presumably why the "equivalently" got written.

## Why it cannot be

`π(I) = 0`, so every positive power vanishes and the filtration collapses to two
strata: everything in degree `0`, nothing above. A grading with at most one
nonzero graded piece cannot reproduce `gbDepth`, which already takes two values
on the partitions of `4` (`gbDepth [4] = 4`, `gbDepth [2,2] = 3`).

## Scope

**Scope-(b), narrowly.** This is a *structural exclusion* — a proved invariant
forbids the construction — but of **one clause**, not of the proposition. What
is excluded is the "equivalently" half of Step 2. The other two objects the
corpus calls `J^•` are untouched:

* **rewrite depth** — Step 2's *first* sentence, "elements requiring at least
  `ℓ` applications of `R_H` / `R_YB`". Not a filtration by ideals, so nothing
  here reaches it. Its own well-definedness is the open question: the phrase
  describes a *word*, and the minimum over words representing a given element is
  `0` for every element, since every element has a normal-form representative.
  So it needs a **chosen** normal form as part of the data, not just a rank
  function.
* **Coxeter length** — `F_ℓ = span{T_w : ℓ(w) ≤ ℓ}`, the independent definition
  in `alg:mba-step07-gb-filtration`. This one *is* well defined (Matsumoto), and
  is excluded for a completely different reason: a dimension count. It fails at
  `n ≤ 3` and holds from `n = 4`. See
  [`2026-08-16-three-gb-filtrations-one-name`](../../../../../docs/audits/2026-08-16-three-gb-filtrations-one-name.md).

**This file is not evidence that the bridge is false**, and none of the above
bears on any mass result. Step 2's *conclusion* may well survive on the rewrite
reading alone; what is dead is the equivalence, and with it Step 3 as written,
since Step 3 chains through both.
-/

namespace QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration

variable {A : Type*} [Ring A] (I : Ideal A) [I.IsTwoSided]

/-- The image of the defining ideal in the quotient is zero.

Not deep — it is what "quotient by `I`" means — but it is the whole obstruction,
and stating it is what stops the free route being taken by accident. -/
theorem map_defining_ideal_eq_bot :
    Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) I = ⊥ :=
  Ideal.map_mk_eq_bot_of_le le_rfl

/-- **Every positive power of the image vanishes.** So the filtration
`J^k := π(I)^k` has `J^0 = A/I` and `J^k = 0` for all `k ≥ 1`. -/
theorem map_pow_eq_bot {k : ℕ} (hk : k ≠ 0) :
    (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) I) ^ k = ⊥ := by
  rw [map_defining_ideal_eq_bot]
  exact Ideal.bot_pow hk

/-- **The associated graded is concentrated in degree `0`.** Every graded piece
`J^k / J^{k+1}` with `k ≥ 1` is the zero quotient, since both terms are `⊥`. -/
theorem graded_piece_trivial {k : ℕ} (hk : k ≠ 0) :
    (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) I) ^ k
      = (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) I) ^ (k + 1) := by
  rw [map_pow_eq_bot I hk, map_pow_eq_bot I (Nat.succ_ne_zero k)]

/-! ### The contradiction with the partition side -/

open QOU.BraidKnot

/-- **The ideal-power filtration cannot carry the partition grading.**

Formally: any function `d` on Young diagrams that is read off a filtration whose
graded pieces above degree `0` all vanish is *constant* on the diagrams that
appear — but `gbDepth` is not constant on the partitions of `4`.

Stated as the implication rather than as a bare `≠` so that the hypothesis is
visible: what a filtration with one nonzero stratum can supply is a *constant*,
and `gbDepth` is not one.

**The step from `map_pow_eq_bot` to this theorem's `hconst` is prose, not
Lean.** Closing it in Lean would need `Z(H_n(q))` and the central idempotents
`e_λ` as actual Lean objects, so that "the grading `Z^{(k)}` read off the
filtration" is a definition rather than a description; neither exists in the
tree. So the two halves are each proved and the join between them is an
argument — which is exactly the epistemic status the audit assigns to the
bridge itself, and it would be dishonest to present this file as more. The real
content is `gbDepth_ne_on_H4`; this theorem is the connector, and it is cheap. -/
theorem gbDepth_not_from_single_stratum
    (d : YoungDiagram → ℕ) (hconst : ∀ μ ν : YoungDiagram, d μ = d ν) :
    d ≠ gbDepth := by
  intro hd
  have := hconst p4 p22
  rw [hd] at this
  exact gbDepth_ne_on_H4 this

end QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration
